WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.636
-Our next guest is a very
talented actress who stars in

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.071
the Apple TV+ show
"Mythic Quest."

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.774
New episodes stream on
Apple TV+ Fridays.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.008
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.710
-Why did you think
that I needed cheering up?

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.347
-Oh, well,
'cause your family hates you

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.615
and you have nowhere to go.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.184
-Where did you get that from?
My family love me.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.285
They, just --
They're in Melbourne.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.254
It's a 16-hour flight, so...

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.189
-They went to Hawaii
and didn't invite you.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.025
-Yes, but the Airbnb
had limited beds,

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.561
and so, we all -- On the
group chat, they told me --

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.797
-There was a two-day layover
in San Diego.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.099
-Whatever. You're spending
Christmas alone, too.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.068
-Well, I don't really do family.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.537
-Uh, more like
family doesn't do you.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.938
Ask your son.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.976
-Please welcome to the show
Charlotte Nicdao, everybody.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.978
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.125
-Hi!
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.161
-I'm so happy to be here.
Thanks for having me.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.463
-Yeah. You're welcome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:07.166
This is a very funny show
about the world of

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:08.600
video-game developing.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.238
How much did you know
about gaming and game design?

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.372
-Not a lot.
-Okay.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:14.841
-I'm ashamed to say.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:18.444
I did -- It was not a world
that I was super-familiar with.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.546
-I don't think you have to be
ashamed about that, FYI.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:21.881
-Oh, good. Thank you.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.582
You know what?
I'm letting the shame go then.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:24.650
It's gone. Yeah.
-Great. You know what?

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.953
That's the least
we can do for you.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.087
-Okay, so I'm done here now.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.189
-Yeah, absolutely.
Thank you. I'm sorry.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.323
I didn't think
it would be this fast.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.791
-Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.793
-Did you have to --
Did you enjoy the research?

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.027
-I really did.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:38.698
You know, right after
I got cast on the show,

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.699
I had to go back to Australia.

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:42.368
And I was like, "I'm going to
get some research done

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.238
while I'm here before I go back
and shoot the first season."

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.074
And I went for a check-up with
my doctor, and she was like,

00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:50.710
"Hey, you know how you got
that pap smear

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.844
before you went to L.A.?

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.112
You failed."
-Oh, wow.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.414
-It was a bad one.
-Okay.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.482
-And I was like --

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.749
-I didn't know they
were pass/fail.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.152
-I didn't know either.
It was a shock to me.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.987
She was like,
"You got to go to hospital.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.055
They're putting you under
a general anesthetic.

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.557
And there gonna,
like, sort that out."

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.226
And I was like,
"Okay, I don't want to do that.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.327
I'm afraid."

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.162
And my husband was like,
"You have to."

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.431
This is an
important lesson, guys.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.932
You got to take care of
your health.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.834
He was like, "You have to.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.702
If you go and do this thing

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:18.404
and go under
your general anesthetic,

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:22.809
on the way home,
we can buy a Nintendo Switch."

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.744
Like, bribing me
like I'm a child.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.981
I was like, "Alright.
Fine, let's go."

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.517
So I went.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.984
I went under
the general anesthetic.

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.552
I woke up -- I don't know if --

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:34.821
Have you ever been
under general anesthetic before?

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.222
-Yes.
-It's really scary.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.390
-It is.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.092
-You do the countdown
and then you get to five

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.195
and then you wake up
and you think you're in

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.697
"Grey's Anatomy,"
which is what I said to

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.866
the lovely nurse
who was standing by me.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.968
I was like,
"I'm in 'Grey's Anatomy.'"

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.771
-And she was like, "No, no,
you're just in the hospital."

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.939
I was like, "Where's my doctor?"

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:56.609
And she was like,
"He's doing another surgery."

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.278
I was like, "What's his name?"

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.147
She was like, "Dr. Derek."

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.284
"Like Grey's Anatomy'?!"

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.418
And she was like,
"Yeah, look, you seem fine.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.919
I'm gonna go."

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:07.953
I was like, "Wait, wait, wait.
I've got to tell you something.

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.155
I've got to tell you something.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.856
She was like,
"What do you have to tell me?

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:16.929
I was like, "On the way home,
I'm getting a Nintendo Switch."

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.831
And then I sat on the couch
for way longer

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.533
than I really needed to playing
my Nintendo Switch.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.800
-Well, you're wonderful
in the show,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.302
so any research
you put into it --

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.871
-No, that was
a really important part of

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.005
the character development, yeah.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.306
-Absolutely.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:30.342
Now, I know your father is
an actor, as well.

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:32.278
So you came from
a family that's in the arts.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.480
Has he been able to come --
Has he visited set?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.550
-Yeah, he came out
when we were shooting Season 1.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.953
And, like,
he's such a character.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.423
He's extremely charismatic.
It's kind of annoying.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.191
It's like, every time
I introduce him

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:48.027
to one of my friends,
he ends up being one of

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.097
their friends
and I'm, like, Al's daughter.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.565
And I brought him on set,
and we were shooting

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.668
kind of a serious scene
at the end of the season.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:58.104
And I went off to shoot
this dramatic scene.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:01.373
And I came back ready to see
my dad be really proud of me.

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:04.143
And he was standing in front of
the monitor, like,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.980
doing a stand-up routine for all
the producers at video village.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.049
And I was like, "Dad, sit down."

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.784
-Well, I'm sure
he's also very proud of you.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.552
But you know when an actor
gets an audience,

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.454
they have to perform.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.856
-He's -- After he left,
all the producers were like,

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:19.458
"We see where you get it from."

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:20.827
-Oh, that's very nice.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.428
But that wasn't
your original plan.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.164
You were going to be
an orchestral clarinetist?

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:29.068
-Yeah. I studied music,
like, for a long time.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.103
I very seriously wanted to be
a musician.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.705
-Whoo!
-Yeah, whoo! Music!

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.674
Lots of music fans
in the crowd tonight.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.542
-Were you a
very talented clarinetist?

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.277
-No, I was not good.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.545
That's the main reason
I didn't --

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.913
-That's the main reason you
got out of it? Yeah.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.049
-I need a lot of praise,
you know?

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.416
And I wasn't getting enough.

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:45.951
I was like, "Where can I go
where I get, like,

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.353
a lot of compliments
all the time"?

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:50.356
-Yeah, everything I've seen
about orchestral musicians,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.224
you never see them
getting a lot of praise.

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:53.492
-No, no.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:55.194
They get, like,
that huge applause

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:59.799
at the end of a performance,
and then, I mean, is that it?

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.768
-Yeah, I think that's about it.
-That's that all I ever got.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.902
I got, like, an obligatory clap,
and then people would be like,

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:05.037
"Okay, that's enough.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.505
Get off the stage."

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.175
-But you also -- It should be
noted you also were in a band.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.342
-I was, yes.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:11.644
-What was the
name of your group?

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.213
-It's called Charlotte Nicdao
and the Sloth Orchestra.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.248
-The Sloth Orchestra?
-Uh-huh.

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:18.984
-And what were the
Sloth Orchestra shows like?

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:21.687
-Well, my whole thing
with this band was that

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.157
I had studied classical and then
jazz music very seriously

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:26.492
for a very long time.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.094
After I decided not to do that
anymore, I was like,

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:32.364
"Like, what's the most fun
version of being a musician?"

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.033
And it was
drinking a lot of wine,

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.467
which I think you can see.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.102
One of those photos,
I'm raising a glass.

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.604
-Yeah, It should be noted,

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.439
not trying to
keep it on the down low.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.841
-This is not a sober woman.
-No, no, that is not.

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:45.778
-It was like a big party where
I would, like, sing like

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.880
I was a toddler with a crown on.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.048
-Yeah.
-It was a lot of fun.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.150
-That's a big difference,
again, to go back --

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.818
I've never seen an
orchestral clarinetist

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:53.886
have a glass of wine with that.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.054
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.657
-Well, you can't.
It will mess up your reed, Seth.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.358
-It will mess up your reed. See?

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.260
You obviously know a lot more
about music than I do.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.763
-That's all that I know.
-You had a cool thing --

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.931
-Reeds.

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.365
-You got to day one,
where they were like,

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:07.933
"And, obviously,
this goes without saying.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.969
The wine will
mess up your reed."

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:12.605
This is pretty cool.
Explain this real quick.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:15.808
-So, this season's
small spoiler alert.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.142
-Small.
-Small, small.

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:20.079
-Allowable spoiler.
-Tiny. I cleared it.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.782
We do an episode where you see
my character, Poppy,

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:25.718
as a young child
growing up in Australia,

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:29.121
which is really exciting to get
to watch the team put together,

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:31.590
because they made a family
that looked just like

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.627
my Australian-Filipino family,
which was really cool.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.296
And the actress that they cast
to play Poppy's mom

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:39.331
is actually
a really close friend of mine,

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:40.466
Hayley Magnus.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.701
She -- I was a bridesmaid
at her wedding.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.570
This is us at
her bachelorette party.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.240
And now when we hang out,
we call it mother-daughter time.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.842
-That's really great.

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:52.211
That's, like, borderline creepy,
but mostly really great.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.313
-It's kind of creepy
and kind of sweet.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:56.649
-You're so wonderful in the
show, which I love a great deal,

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:57.750
and I'm so happy
to have you here.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.784
Thank you so much
for making time for us.

00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:00.118
-Thank you so much.

00:07:00.118 --> 00:07:02.688
-You guys,
that's Charlotte Nicdao.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.958
New episodes of "Mythic Quest"
stream Fridays on Apple TV+.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:10.530
We'll be right back.

